From 6209e35762f5fcd4abdc6653e3fe7fd049ae4f67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emil Boenke <boenkeemil@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:11:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] German spelling: de-DE, de-AT, de-CH with Hunspell
 compounding
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

German was hyphenated but never spell-checked, so German text was flagged
against the US English word list.

- affix engine: Hunspell compounding (COMPOUNDFLAG, COMPOUNDBEGIN/MIDDLE/END,
  COMPOUNDPERMITFLAG, COMPOUNDFORBIDFLAG, ONLYINCOMPOUND, COMPOUNDMIN,
  COMPOUNDWORDMAX), NEEDAFFIX/PSEUDOROOT, CIRCUMFIX, CHECKSHARPS; homonyms kept
  apart in compounding dictionaries; flags named only in continuation classes
  count; MAP groups with multi-letter items become REP pairs.
- new `de` proofing module: Germany, Austria, Switzerland, each reading its own
  installed Hunspell dictionary (LibreOffice `*_frami` too), German messages,
  umlaut/ß suggestions, German repeated-word and spacing checks.
- new documents follow the region's German (German interface, or English
  interface on a German-speaking system): de-AT on an Austrian Windows.
- dictionaries are also looked up in a `dictionaries` folder beside the program.
- Language dialog and region list offer German (Austria) and (Switzerland).

